* DATA declares a PERSON record and a NAME selector.
* GREET is a separate function that receives the record as an argument and concatenates the greeting with NAME(P).
    DATA('PERSON(NAME)')
    DEFINE('GREET(P)')
    P = PERSON('Zuriel')
    OUTPUT = GREET(P) :(END)
GREET GREET = 'Hi ' NAME(P) :(RETURN)
END
